16 0 obj
<< /A 43 0 R /Alt (Infographic illustrating the three forms of autophagy: macroautophagy, microautophagy, and chaperone-mediated autophagy, each with stepwise diagrams and key features including cargo type, mechanism, membrane source, and selectivity.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 27 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 44 0 R /Alt (Infographic summarizes how chaperone-mediated autophagy \(CMA\) drives cancer hallmarks such as proliferation, growth suppression, cell death resistance, immortality, angiogenesis, metabolism, plasticity, immune evasion, and metastasis. Central diagram illustrates CMA\220s core mechanism and peripheral panels explain its roles in each hallmark using color-coded sections with icons, pathways, and concise text describing protein regulation, degradation, and functional consequences for tumor progression.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 30 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
